<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The DAF Under Writing mark, as an animated SVG ("Assemble").  THE one copy.

    t-called by the webclient boot overlay (views/boot_loader_templates.xml).
    Callers supply their own wrapper, because the accessible label differs by
    surface:

        <div class="m-daf-loader" role="status" aria-label="Chargement">
            <t t-call="daf_uw_theme.daf_mark"/>
        </div>

    Choreography (keyframes in static/src/scss/loader.scss): the D's outline is
    drawn then filled, the A rises out of a blur, the F's black arm and blue
    bar slide together, the triangle spins in, the tagline is wiped in, then a
    light sweep runs over the glossy letters for as long as the wait lasts.

    ⚠ GENERATED GEOMETRY.  Every `d`, gradient and highlight stroke below is
    copied from static/src/img/brand/daf_uw_logo.svg; only the ids are
    namespaced (m-daf-*) so nothing can collide with an Odoo selector.  Change
    the brand SVG and regenerate; do not hand-edit coordinates here.

    ⚠ ANIMATION CLASSES SIT ON THE <use> ELEMENTS, NEVER ON THE <path>s IN
    <defs>.  Gecko does not reflect an animation on a referenced element into
    its <use> instances (the old tree mark froze as a static logo on every
    Firefox because of exactly this).  Geometry lives in <defs> once, unstyled.

    The <defs> ids are not namespaced per caller.  Two instances on one page
    would collide, and that is harmless by construction: both resolve to the
    same geometry.
-->
